== create aetherproxy table (same shapes as aether-proxy's nft.uc)

== 1. query members of chnroute4 over netlink (no nft CLI)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset dump inet@aetherproxy@chnroute4
set inet@aetherproxy@chnroute4: 3 messages, 5 elements, errors=[]
  1.0.1.0 - 1.0.3.255
  223.255.252.0 - 223.255.253.255
(2 members, sentinel=true)

== 2. per-IP membership test (what tag:none needs)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset test inet@aetherproxy@chnroute4 1.0.1.5
test 1.0.1.5: FOUND (43.791µs)

+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset test inet@aetherproxy@chnroute4 1.0.4.1
test 1.0.4.1: NOT_FOUND errno=-2 (No such file or directory) (42.251µs)

== 3. add a batch to gfw4 (interval begin+end, batch begin/end, one ACK)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add inet@aetherproxy@gfw4 10.2.0.1 10.2.0.2 10.2.0.3
add 3 ip(s): ACK_OK (88.753µs)

+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset dump inet@aetherproxy@gfw4
set inet@aetherproxy@gfw4: 3 messages, 6 elements, errors=[]
  10.2.0.1 - 10.2.0.1
  10.2.0.2 - 10.2.0.2
  10.2.0.3 - 10.2.0.3
(3 members, sentinel=false)

== 3b. nft CLI after chinadns-ng-style consecutive raw adds (known upstream interaction)
-- nft list still works:
table inet aetherproxy {
	set gfw4 {
		type ipv4_addr
		flags interval
		auto-merge
		elements = { 10.2.0.1, 10.2.0.2,
			     10.2.0.3 }
	}
}
-- nft add element fails (same with the real chinadns-ng binary):
netlink: Error: Could not process rule: No such file or directory
nft add rc=1
-- direct netlink add still works:
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add inet@aetherproxy@gfw4 10.2.0.4
add 1 ip(s): ACK_OK (53.292µs)

== 4. exact duplicate add is idempotent (no NLM_F_EXCL)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add inet@aetherproxy@gfw4 10.2.0.1
add 1 ip(s): ACK_OK (48.471µs)

== 5. adding an IP inside an existing range fails EEXIST (whole batch aborts)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add inet@aetherproxy@eexist4 1.2.3.88 10.8.8.8
add 2 ip(s): ERROR errno=-17 (File exists) (38.684428ms)

+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset dump inet@aetherproxy@eexist4
set inet@aetherproxy@eexist4: 3 messages, 3 elements, errors=[]
  1.2.3.0 - 1.2.3.255
(1 members, sentinel=true)

== 6. chinadns-ng-style test-then-add avoids EEXIST
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add-safe inet@aetherproxy@eexist4 1.2.3.99 10.9.9.9
add-safe 2 ip(s): added 1 missing (1 round(s)) (120.224µs)

+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset dump inet@aetherproxy@eexist4
set inet@aetherproxy@eexist4: 3 messages, 5 elements, errors=[]
  1.2.3.0 - 1.2.3.255
  10.9.9.9 - 10.9.9.9
(2 members, sentinel=true)

== 7. benchmark (one process, one socket, no shell-outs)
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset bench-test inet@aetherproxy@chnroute4 1.0.1.5 1000
bench-test n=1000 hits=1000 total=5.166943ms per_op=5.166µs

+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset bench-add inet@aetherproxy@uproxy4 500
bench-add n=500 total=2.078468ms per_ip=4.156µs

== 8. failure modes
-- missing set
+ sudo ip netns exec m0-nftset /workspace/openwrt/aether-dns/spikes/m0-nftset/target/release/m0-nftset add inet@aetherproxy@nope 10.1.1.1
add 1 ip(s): ERROR errno=-2 (No such file or directory) (16.678559ms)

-- no CAP_NET_ADMIN
